  "assembly": {
    "id": "body-exterior",
    "name": "Exterior — 5-door, white, R styling",
    "system": "body",
    "origin": [
      0,
      0.13,
      0
    ],
    "description": "The operator's car outside (dossier §1): 5-door in white, with the R signatures — deeper front bumper with enlarged intakes, rear bumper with diffuser framing the quad tips, roof spoiler, gloss-black mirror caps, side skirts. L≈4,268 mm, W 1,799 mm, H≈1,470 mm in real life; the model wraps the compressed scene chassis. Hide Body systems via the tree to get the mechanical view back. R11 paint block: the UK pre-facelift R's standard solid white is PURE WHITE, L-code LC9A, sticker code 0Q0Q (the other white was Oryx White Mother-of-Pearl) — the operator should confirm LC9A on the service book / boot-floor sticker. Replacement panels come GRU (grey-primed)."
